ALL=[(r[:2]+('STR marketplace and optional buyer assistance','https://rabbu.com/about',)+r[4:6]+('Rabbu describes a marketplace, market and revenue tools, agent and lender connections, and optional search consultants from market selection through closing. Tools and done-for-you help are different service levels; obtain the scope for the one you intend to use.',)+r[7:]) if r[0]=='rabbu' else r for r in ALL]
# Each alternatives guide has an original, provider-specific decision exercise.
EXERCISES={
 'the-short-term-shop':('Brokerage representation versus project coordination','Make two columns for one selected market: the agent’s representation agreement and the acquisition coordinator’s scope. Put legal-use verification, the revenue memo, insurance quotes, furnishing orders and opening readiness under a named person. Brokerage can be sufficient if your other specialists are already selected. Pay for extra coordination only where the proposal closes a real gap.', ['Signed representation terms','Address-level decision memo','Named launch coordinator']),
 'techvestor':('Portfolio exposure versus one-property control','Compare a portfolio subscription with a direct purchase using the same amount of available capital. The portfolio case needs distribution policy, liquidity restrictions and investor rights. The property case needs cash to launch, reserves, an operator and an exit estimate. Do not assume a portfolio interest gives you control over a specific house or that a single house offers diversification.', ['Offering and subscription documents','Distribution and redemption policy','Direct-property cash and operator plan']),
 'airdna':('Forecast confidence versus executed diligence','Choose one active listing and recreate its revenue estimate using comparable properties of similar bedroom count, legal occupancy, location and amenities. Then add address-specific taxes, insurance, repairs, HOA charges, financing and management. A data subscription is enough only when you can perform and coordinate those remaining checks before contingencies expire.', ['Comparable listing set','Address-specific expense quotes','Offer and contingency calendar']),
 'rabbu':('Free research versus a paid search engagement','Screen a listing with the marketplace and calculator, then request the scope of any optional search consultant. Mark which assumptions are estimates and which have been checked against records. Require a named owner for permit questions, inspections and closing tasks. Compare the paid tier with another written acquisition proposal rather than equating every tool user with a managed purchase client.', ['Exact tier and compensation disclosure','Verified versus estimated inputs','Search and closing deliverables']),
 'awning':('Connected search and management versus independent vendors','Ask the buying contact and the management contact to quote the same address. Separate representation costs from setup, recurring management charges and excluded services. Confirm availability with the actual local operator and ask whether buying assistance depends on a management contract. Choose a connected provider only if both contracts suit the property and your intended control.', ['Local coverage confirmation','Acquisition and management agreements','Fee base and termination rights']),
 'bnb-mastery':('Operating skill versus property ownership','Write your desired outcome before selecting a program: buying a deed, leasing with permission to sublet, or managing someone else’s rental. Those require different capital and agreements. A co-hosting course can suit a service-business goal without being an acquisition alternative. If ownership is the goal, retain a lender-approved budget and a buyer-owned purchase schedule.', ['Desired ownership or business model','Current curriculum and coaching scope','Property-purchase capital plan']),
 'robuilt':('Creative development versus buying an existing home','Take one distinctive-stay concept and one existing rental candidate. The development case needs land-use feasibility, construction quotes, utility access and holding costs through opening. The existing-home case needs permission, condition, furnishing gaps and a transition plan. Coaching can develop your project skill; it does not remove those costs or transfer project responsibility.', ['Permits and utility feasibility','Build or repair quotes','Zero-revenue holding budget']),
 'rent-to-retirement':('Inventory purchase versus an STR-specific search','Select one available inventory property and one independently sourced STR candidate. Confirm the permitted rental use and model each using its own income and expenses. Identify who is paid by the seller, who provides representation and whether management is tied to purchase. A packaged long-term rental may fit your plan better; never convert its advertised numbers into an Airbnb forecast.', ['Inventory and seller disclosures','Rental-use-specific underwriting','Independent condition and value checks']),
 'alpha-geek-capital':('An offering interest versus a directly selected asset','Compare the exact fund or single-asset offering with buying an individual house. List voting rights, financing liability, operating control, capital calls and exit authority on both sides. An LLC interest can confer economic ownership without unilateral authority over sale or refinancing. Your advisers should read the documents before you value any potential tax allocation.', ['Current offering terms','Control and capital-call provisions','Exit and reporting rules']),
 'elk-ridge-investments':('Managed participation versus your own purchase','Map the actual deed, owning entity and investor interest before comparing either proposal. Request voting, capital-call, distribution and exit provisions for participation. For a direct purchase, document your financing and operator choices. If being able to choose or sell one property is essential, resolve that right before comparing projected income or depreciation.', ['Ownership and governing documents','Capital-call and exit provisions','Named operator and reporting duties']),
 'str-search':('What counts as a completed property match?','Define four milestones: screened listing, buyer approval, accepted offer and live rental. Have the provider place its obligations and any match conditions next to each. A listing can match a model and still fail inspection, insurance or legal-use checks. Your agreement should show who resolves that failure and what support remains when the first candidate is rejected.', ['Matching criteria and remedy','Deal evidence and rejected-property rules','Closing and launch responsibility map']),
 'bnb-turnkey':('A management transition you can actually control','Assume you need to change managers six months after opening. Walk through account permissions, payout access, cleaner contacts, furniture ownership, future bookings and vendor contracts. Obtain the actual termination notice, fees and transfer process. A combined-looking pitch is useful only when the acquisition and operating agreements work together without unclear lock-in.', ['Management entity and fee base','Account and record access','Termination and handoff provisions']),
 'kleer-circle':('Your first-year operating capacity','Build a seven-day duty roster for guest messages, cleaning inspections, repairs, pricing and payout reconciliation. Put a primary and backup person next to each, including holiday coverage. Price those services instead of treating automation as zero labor. If you cannot staff the roster, confirm a management exception or compare another operating model before offering.', ['Buyer and backup duty roster','Actual software and vendor costs','Written management-change terms']),
 'str-insights':('Which product buys accountability?','Put the portal, consultation and acquisition proposal on separate rows. For each, ask who checks an address, who prepares a complete model, who attends the inspection decision and who tracks closing and opening. Select the least extensive tier that covers your gaps. A screen full of deals is useful research, but does not alone establish contract-to-close responsibility.', ['Exact product tier','Deliverables and exclusions','Named transaction and launch owners']),
 'michael-elefante':('Mentorship outputs versus completed tasks','Ask a mentor to define what happens when you submit a live listing: feedback call, edited model, permit-check review or actual execution. Then compare that with an acquisition service’s delivered documents and coordination. Choose education if you want to build repeatable skills and have time to execute; choose professional help for specific work you cannot staff.', ['Current support and curriculum','Actual-deal feedback process','Buyer execution calendar']),
 'real-estate-robinsons':('Choose the product, not just the public brand','Separate Alpha Host mentorship, public resources, design or cleaning services and an investment offer. The same public brand can link to products with very different obligations. Write down the legal entity, promised output and customer work for the exact product quoted. Do not infer acquisition execution from a coaching, event or design purchase.', ['Exact product and contracting entity','Promised output and exclusions','Purchase and launch responsibilities']),
 'str-university':('Confirm active support before buying education','Use the course page as a starting point and request current dates, curriculum updates, support contact and refund terms. A historical cohort announcement is not evidence of a live intake. If a listing is already under contract, confirm whether help can arrive before the diligence deadline; otherwise hire the appropriate specialist for that decision.', ['Current enrollment confirmation','Curriculum update and support details','Deadline-specific professional help']),
 'str-profit-academy':('Historical program name versus today’s offer','Identify the current seller and product before paying for something described in an old episode. Get today’s curriculum, support, price and cancellation terms in writing. If the goal is buying now, compare the current offer’s actual-deal feedback with an acquisition proposal. Historical success stories do not establish present service availability.', ['Current seller and contract','Active support and refund terms','Work performed on your actual deal']),
}
