CONTRACTS={
 'elk-ridge-investments':('Elk Ridge Investments Ownership & Exit Questions','/guides/elk-ridge-investments-ownership-questions/','Read the actual ownership documents before joining a managed STR participation arrangement.', [
 ('What exactly will I own?','Request the deed, entity chart, subscription or purchase agreement and governing documents. Identify whether you hold a direct property interest, an LLC interest or another arrangement. Marketing language about ownership participation does not settle that question.'),
 ('Who can commit more capital?','Identify capital-call authority, payment deadlines, dilution or default remedies and limits on borrowing. Ask whether you can decline additional funding and what happens to the existing investment if you do.'),
 ('Who chooses the exit?','Record sale, refinance and redemption rights separately. Ask whether an investor can request an exit, what approval is required, which charges apply and how value is determined. A proposed exit schedule is different from an enforceable liquidity right.'),
 ('What reporting reaches my advisers?','Request a sample investor report, financial statements and a tax-reporting timetable. Have your own CPA assess eligibility and allocation questions from the actual documents; K-1 issuance alone does not establish usable personal tax deductions.')]),
 'str-search':('STR Search Property Match: Questions Before Signing','/guides/str-search-property-match-questions/','Translate a property-match pitch into screening criteria, evidence and enforceable deliverables.', [
 ('What counts as a match?','Write down budget, market, property type, financing, legal use and acceptable downside. Ask what milestone satisfies the service: delivery of a listing, buyer acceptance, an offer or a closing. Confirm conditions and any remedy in the agreement.'),
 ('What happens when a matched house fails diligence?','Request rejected-deal examples and rules for a property that fails insurance, inspections, permit checks or lender approval. Ask whether another search is included and whether the service period or fee changes.'),
 ('Can I recreate the revenue model?','Ask for the comparable set, monthly seasonality, adjustments, expense base and sensitivity case. Treat a model as an estimate and connect important seller claims to records. Ask who revises the model when quotes or inspection findings change.'),
 ('Who owns closing and launch?','Assign representation, inspection decisions, contingency deadlines, furnishing orders and opening readiness to named parties. Identify included coordination versus introductions. A matching service need not cover all of those tasks.')]),
 'bnb-turnkey':('BNB Turnkey Management & Handoff Questions','/guides/bnb-turnkey-management-handoff/','Price the operating agreement and preserve access before choosing a connected acquisition path.', [
 ('Which company manages the property?','Get the legal name and local contact from the actual agreement. Confirm market availability, authority over pricing and vendor selection, and emergency coverage. A named partner in marketing does not establish your contract.'),
 ('What is the fee charged on?','Request gross versus net definitions, cleaning-fee treatment, minimum charges, onboarding, supplies, maintenance markups and excluded services. Use the same revenue case when comparing a separate operator.'),
 ('Who owns accounts and records?','Document listing control, access to booking and payout records, photography rights and software subscriptions. Confirm what remains accessible after termination and who handles existing guests during transfer.'),
 ('How do I change operators?','Read notice periods, termination charges, booking obligations and vendor handoff duties. Test a hypothetical transition six months after opening before committing to the purchase-and-management combination.')]),
 'kleer-circle':('Kleer Circle Year-One Self-Management Questions','/guides/kleer-circle-year-one-operations/','Test whether the year-one operating model fits your time and backup coverage.', [
 ('What work stays with me?','Ask for the daily and weekly duty list behind the operating playbook: guest responses, cleaners, repairs, pricing and bookkeeping. Identify service targets and what the systems automate versus what a person must decide.'),
 ('Who covers nights and holidays?','Name a local primary and backup for lockouts, heating failures and cleaning issues. Get actual availability and prices. A configured messaging system cannot itself repair a failed heater.'),
 ('What does self-operation really cost?','Budget software, cleaning quality checks, maintenance dispatch, backup coverage and buyer time. Compare that case with a written manager quote. Keep labor assumptions separate from provider fees.'),
 ('Can I change the year-one model?','The public FAQ describes first-year buyer operation and management introductions later. Ask for any exception in writing, who approves it, which support changes and what additional costs apply. Ask your own CPA how the actual work pattern affects your situation.')]),
 'str-insights':('STR Insights Portal vs Acquisition Service Questions','/guides/str-insights-service-tiers/','Select a tier by delivered work and accountability, not by the number of listings available.', [
 ('Which tier am I paying for?','Have the proposal name portal access, consultation, property finding or acquisition-and-launch execution explicitly. A description on another service page is not evidence that it is included in your purchase.'),
 ('Who checks a candidate address?','Identify responsibility for legal-use questions, condition, comparable selection and lender assumptions. Ask which checks are performed versus referred to specialists and how findings reach the buyer.'),
 ('Who acts while the contract is live?','List the agent, inspector, lender and acquisition coordinator next to each deadline. Ask who updates the model, recommends a repair request and confirms when contingencies are ready to expire.'),
 ('What is delivered at opening?','Request the furnishing scope, invoices, listing-access handoff, pricing setup, operating agreement and unresolved-items list. Clarify support duration and exclusions for the specific service tier.')]),
}
def esc(s):return tpl.esc(s)
def published(path, fallback=DATE):
 p=ROOT/path.strip('/')/'index.html'
 if p.exists():
  m=re.search(r'"datePublished"\s*:\s*"([^"]+)"',p.read_text());return m[1] if m else fallback
 return fallback
def section(h,p):return f'<section class="section-sm"><div class="wrap wrap-narrow"><h2>{esc(h)}</h2>{p}</div></section>'
def page(path,title,desc,body,pub=None):
 trail=[('Home','/'),('Compare','/compare/'),(title,path)]
 schema=tpl.graph(tpl.breadcrumb_schema(trail),tpl.ORG_SCHEMA)+'\n'+tpl.article_schema(title,desc,tpl.SITE+path,pub or published(path),DATE,section='STR Buyer Comparisons')
 write(path,tpl.page(title=title,description=desc,path=path,body=body,extra_schema=schema,active='/compare/',body_class='buyer-compare',transparent=True))
def hero(h,lead,label='First STR buyer comparison'):
 return f'<section class="hero hero-page"><div class="wrap"><a class="bc-back" href="/compare/">← All comparisons</a><div class="hero-inner"><span class="eyebrow">{esc(label)}</span><h1>{esc(h)}</h1><p class="lead">{esc(lead)}</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-accent" href="/apply/">Discuss My First STR</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-light" href="/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/">Check My Purchase Cash</a></div></div></div></section>'
def source(r):
 return f'<p class="bc-source">Published by BNB Accelerator, an acquisition provider with a commercial interest in this comparison. Provider facts summarized from <a href="{esc(r[3])}" rel="noopener noreferrer">{esc(r[1])}’s public material</a>, reviewed {CHECKED[r[0]]}. Availability, fees and agreements may change. This is a public-offer comparison, not a customer review, independent ranking or endorsement. The companies are not affiliated. Verify the actual terms directly.</p>'
def links(r):
 g=CONTRACTS.get(r[0]);more=f' · <a href="{g[1]}">{esc(g[0])}</a>' if g else ''
 return f'<p><a href="{r[4]}">BNB Accelerator vs {esc(r[1])}</a> · <a href="/compare/alternatives-to-{r[0]}/">{esc(r[1])} alternatives</a>{more}</p>'
def alternatives(r):
 slug,name,cat,src,cmp,q,fit,opts,dil=r; h,exercise,records=EXERCISES[slug]
 cards=''.join(f'<article class="bc-option"><span class="eyebrow">Path {i}</span><h3>{esc(n)}</h3><p><strong>Fits:</strong> {esc(w)}</p><p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> {esc(t)}</p></article>' for i,(n,w,t) in enumerate(opts,1))
 body=hero(f'Alternatives to {name}',q,'Alternatives · Purchase decision')
 body+=section('Start with the outcome you need',f'<p>{esc(fit)}</p><p>For a first STR, decide whether you want to select a particular home, own an interest in managed assets, or learn to execute the purchase yourself. These paths involve different control, capital and work. BNB Accelerator coordinates sourcing, underwriting, purchase and launch for a client-approved property; the signed scope defines the work included.</p>')
 body+=f'<section class="bg-alt"><div class="wrap"><h2>Three credible paths to compare</h2><div class="bc-grid">{cards}</div></div></section>'
 body+=section(h,f'<p>{esc(exercise)}</p><div class="bc-docs"><h3>Build this decision file</h3><ol>'+''.join(f'<li>{esc(x)}</li>' for x in records)+'</ol></div>')
 body+=section('Make the total cash comparable','<p>Use the same property price and current financing terms for direct-purchase proposals. Add down payment, closing, furnishing, repairs, quoted service fees and retained reserves. For an offering, separate the subscription amount from possible future capital obligations and liquidity restrictions. A lower fee is meaningful only when the missing work and buyer responsibilities are visible.</p><p><a href="/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/">Calculate first-STR purchase cash</a> and enter the fees actually quoted to you. Use conservative revenue and address-specific expense evidence; neither a provider’s case study nor potential tax savings funds your down payment.</p>')
 body+=section('Choose before you sign',f'<div class="callout"><p>{esc(dil)}</p></div><p>Proceed when the documents settle that question and the capital, scope and operating plan fit. Request a revision if duties or charges are vague. Pause when legal use, financing, insurance or operator capacity can change the purchase. Compare proposals on the same decision file and keep the right to reject an unsuitable property.</p>{links(r)}{source(r)}')
 body+=tpl.cta_band('Choose support for your first STR','Bring your available cash, target markets and the work you want the team to handle.',primary=('/apply/','Discuss My Purchase'),secondary=('/buy-a-short-term-rental/','First STR Roadmap'))
 page(f'/compare/alternatives-to-{slug}/',f'{name} Alternatives for First STR Buyers',f'Compare alternatives to {name}: service scope, buyer work, ownership and all-in cash. Choose help for your first STR purchase.',body)
def matchup(r):
 slug,name,cat,src,path,q,fit,opts,dil=r
 if path.startswith('/blog/'):return # preserve established, detailed owner URL
 rows=[('Service model','Sourcing, underwriting and purchase-to-launch coordination',cat),('Buyer decision','Client approves the property and commits purchase capital',q),('Work to document','Named purchase, launch and operator handoffs',dil),('Fees','Request current acquisition fee, exclusions and vendor disclosures','Request the actual tier, itemized charges and ongoing terms'),('Evidence','Property-level memo, full cash budget and downside case','Request the records listed below for your exact product')]
 table='<div class="bc-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Provider scope comparison" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Decision</th><th scope="col">BNB Accelerator</th><th scope="col">'+esc(name)+'</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join(f'<{tag}>{esc(v)}</{tag}>' for tag,v in [('th',a),('td',b),('td',c)])+'</tr>' for a,b,c in rows)+'</tbody></table></div>'
 h,exercise,records=EXERCISES[slug]
 body=hero('BNB Accelerator vs '+name,q)
 body+=section('The decision in plain terms',f'<p>{esc(fit)}</p><p>BNB Accelerator’s <a href="/how-it-works/">published process</a> describes coordinating a client-approved purchase and launch. Compare the service you would actually sign for, rather than comparing a brand’s entire website with one proposal. There is no universal winner: ownership rights, the work you want done and your operating capacity decide the fit.</p>')
 body+=f'<section class="section-sm bg-alt"><div class="wrap"><h2>Side-by-side buyer responsibilities</h2>{table}</div></section>'
 body+=section(h,f'<p>{esc(exercise)}</p><h3>Request these records</h3><ul>'+''.join(f'<li>{esc(x)}</li>' for x in records)+'</ul>')
 body+=section('Use one property and one budget','<p>Give each acquisition provider the same active listing, available cash, financing assumptions and intended operating model. Require an address-level permission plan, comparable revenue evidence, an expense model and a maximum offer under a downside case. If you are evaluating education or an offering, compare it to that purpose instead of expecting it to perform a transaction.</p><p>Budget the complete purchase with the <a href="/tools/first-str-purchase-budget/">first-STR cash planner</a>. Verify which professionals you contract with and who monitors contingencies. Financing approval, permits, bookings and investment outcomes remain property- and buyer-specific.</p>')
 body+=section('Which option fits your first purchase?',f'<p>{esc(opts[0][1])} {esc(opts[0][2])}</p><p>{esc(opts[1][1])} {esc(opts[1][2])}</p><p>Choose the proposal that assigns responsibility, explains its model and fits your cash and time limits. Do not sign merely because a sales timeline or tax illustration looks attractive.</p>{links(r)}{source(r)}')
 body+=tpl.cta_band('Test our acquisition scope on your purchase','Bring the same budget and candidate you are discussing with other providers.',primary=('/apply/','Compare My Purchase Plan'),secondary=('/compare/alternatives/','Browse Alternatives'))
 title=f'BNB Accelerator vs {name}: First STR Buyer Guide'
 page(path,title,f'Compare BNB Accelerator and {name} for your first STR: scope, buyer responsibilities, ownership, fees and purchase evidence.',body)
def contract(r):
 if r[0] not in CONTRACTS:return
 title,path,lead,items=CONTRACTS[r[0]]
 body=hero(title,lead,'Before signing · Contract questions')
 body+=section('Turn the proposal into a decision file',f'<p>This guide is for a buyer already considering {esc(r[1])}. It focuses on questions to resolve in the agreement, rather than ranking providers. {esc(r[6])}</p><p>Keep a four-column file: requested record, current answer, responsible person and deadline. An unanswered material question is a decision to defer, not a reason to invent a favorable assumption. Review the actual contract with the appropriate professional before funding.</p>')
 for h,p in items:body+=section(h,f'<p>{esc(p)}</p>')
 # A distinct, usable worksheet belongs to the particular provider's service model.
 rows=''.join(f'<tr><th scope="row">{esc(h)}</th><td>Document / clause / named owner</td><td>Resolved before payment or offer</td></tr>' for h,_ in items)
 body+=f'<section class="section-sm bg-alt"><div class="wrap"><h2>Your proposal review worksheet</h2><div class="bc-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Proposal review worksheet" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Evidence to record</th><th scope="col">Decision gate</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows}</tbody></table></div></div></section>'
 body+=section('Use a missing-answer test','<p>Hypothetical example: the provider has explained its search or participation process, but has not documented who pays an unexpected $12,000 property cost. Keep that item unresolved until the governing agreement or a written scope revision identifies the responsible party and your exposure. Re-run available cash with the actual obligation; do not treat the brochure’s initial amount as a cap.</p><p>Proceed when material rights, duties and costs are documented and fit your plan. Request amendments for vague exclusions. Delay funding or an offer when a missing answer can change control, affordability or legal use. A favorable case study cannot substitute for your agreement.</p>')
 body+=section('Continue your buyer comparison',links(r)+source(r))
 body+=tpl.cta_band('Discuss the work you want done','We can explain our own acquisition scope, budget and professional handoffs.',primary=('/apply/','Discuss My First STR'),secondary=('/guides/str-service-responsibility-matrix/','Map Acquisition Duties'))
 page(path,title,lead,body)
def hubs():
 groups=[('Acquisition, brokerage and purchase platforms',['elk-ridge-investments','str-search','bnb-turnkey','kleer-circle','str-insights','the-short-term-shop','awning','rabbu','rent-to-retirement']),('Managed investment offerings',['techvestor','alpha-geek-capital']),('Education and mentorship',['bnb-mastery','robuilt','michael-elefante','real-estate-robinsons','str-university','str-profit-academy']),('Data for buyers',['airdna'])]
